     1,
     "Hi:\r<br>I am trying to use the cumsum function with the following dataset by\r<br>column,\r<br>problem is, if I use  apply(winter[,2:7],2,cumsum) my &#39;week&#39; column\r<br>dissapears.\r<br>I would like to use ddply along with colwise if possible but can&#39;t get\r<br>right yet.\r<br>If I use:  ddply(winter,.(week),colwise(cumsum)) doesn&#39;t do anything\r<br>because I only\r<br>have one value per week and it only repeats what I already have. This\r<br>seems to be a simple\r<br>task.\r<br>\r<br>winter &lt;- structure(list(week = c(26L, 27L, 28L, 29L, 30L, 31L, 32L,\r<br>33L,\r<br>34L, 35L, 36L, 37L, 38L, 39L, 40L, 41L, 42L, 43L, 44L, 45L, 46L,\r<br>47L, 48L, 49L, 50L, 51L, 52L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 4L, 5L, 6L, 7L, 8L,\r<br>9L, 10L, 11L, 12L, 13L, 14L, 15L, 16L, 17L, 18L, 19L, 20L, 21L,\r<br>22L, 23L, 24L, 25L), BY2010 = c(0L, 0L, 460L, 1126L, 1755L, 11153L,\r<br>27998L, 56336L, 12486L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L,\r<br>0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L,\r<br>0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L,\r<br>0L), BY2009 = c(0L, 95L, 341L, 373L, 2859L, 5769L, 33263L, 98435L,\r<br>345339L, 622621L, 349958L, 531232L, 652803L, 345358L, 142991L,\r<br>148883L, 957501L, 32495L, 14862L, 7210L, 9765L, 6846L, 5067L,\r<br>6201L, 3045L, 106230L, 1183L, 195L, 6855L, 10261L, 4179L, 650L,\r<br>240L, 165L, 1189L, 863L, 562L, 1350L, 188L, 479L, 770L, 0L, 558L,\r<br>314L, 147L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L), BY2008 = c(0L, 0L, 77L,\r<br>124L, 159L, 2376L, 9480L, 17314L, 99574L, 323679L, 198211L, 93630L,\r<br>129183L, 111820L, 71260L, 35241L, 14020L, 20778L, 21694L, 15016L,\r<br>13400L, 9187L, 3607L, 2804L, 2417L, 5291L, 16216L, 898L, 558L,\r<br>709L, 972L, 61L, 372L, 3086L, 10108L, 4295L, 882L, 2593L, 36L,\r<br>233L, 243L, 0L, 70L, 272L, 308L, 134L, 40L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L, 0L\r<br>), BY2007 = c(0L, 0L, 0L, 10775L, 4166L, 4958L, 16221L, 29401L,\r<br>34951L, 33188L, 146044L, 105007L, 185297L, 159682L, 207537L,\r<br>140694L, 128275