     1,
     "<u></u>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div>\n\n\n<p><font size=\"2\">Deear Felipe,<br>\n<br>\nThis is more a general R-help question than a ggplot2 question...<br>\n<br>\nThe week column &#39;disappears&#39; in your apply code because to tell it to disappear. Have a look at str(winter[, 2:7])<br>\n<br>\nYou just need to cbind week to the result of apply()<br>\n<br>\ncbind(winter[, 1, drop = FALSE], apply(winter[,-1], 2, cumsum))<br>\n<br>\nAnother option<br>\n<br>\ncumsumwinter &lt;- winter<br>\ncumsumwinter[, -1] &lt;- apply(cumsumwinter[, -1], 2, cumsum)<br>\n<br>\nBest regards,<br>\n<br>\nThierry<br>\n<br>\n-----Oorspronkelijk bericht-----<br>\nVan: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> namens Felipe<br>\nVerzonden: vr 27-8-2010 23:48<br>\nAan: ggplot2<br>\nOnderwerp: cumsum</font></p></div>"
    ],
    [
